WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:02.911
MyCampusView Academy.

2
00:00:02.961 --> 00:00:06.397
AI for Young Builders, video 5.

3
00:00:06.447 --> 00:00:09.320
Train your first AI model.

4
00:00:10.450 --> 00:00:11.526
Time to build!

5
00:00:11.576 --> 00:00:16.433
In this lesson you will train an image classifier: an AI that

6
00:00:16.483 --> 00:00:19.490
sorts drawings into groups you choose.

7
00:00:20.850 --> 00:00:22.735
There are four steps.

8
00:00:22.785 --> 00:00:27.619
Choose your groups, like circle, triangle and square.

9
00:00:27.669 --> 00:00:30.936
Draw at least five examples of each.

10
00:00:30.986 --> 00:00:32.042
Press Train.

11
00:00:32.092 --> 00:00:37.110
Then draw something new and see what your model thinks.

12
00:00:38.450 --> 00:00:42.013
Here is the secret to a smart model: variety.

13
00:00:42.063 --> 00:00:46.990
Draw some shapes big and some small, some neat and some messy,

14
00:00:47.040 --> 00:00:49.720
in different places on the canvas.

15
00:00:49.770 --> 00:00:55.580
The more kinds of example it sees, the better it copes with new drawings.

16
00:00:56.950 --> 00:01:01.184
When you test a drawing, the model shows its confidence.

17
00:01:01.234 --> 00:01:05.392
Here it is sixty-seven percent sure this is a triangle.

18
00:01:05.442 --> 00:01:12.200
Low confidence means the drawing sits between groups, and your model needs more examples.

19
00:01:13.550 --> 00:01:18.946
If your model mixes two groups up, add more examples of both,

20
00:01:18.996 --> 00:01:23.500
especially the kind it got wrong, then train again.

21
00:01:23.550 --> 00:01:27.607
Test, find mistakes, add better data, retrain.

22
00:01:27.657 --> 00:01:32.250
That loop is exactly what AI engineers do every day.

23
00:01:33.550 --> 00:01:38.513
Your model trains right in your browser, so your drawings are not

24
00:01:38.563 --> 00:01:40.518
sent anywhere to train it.

25
00:01:40.568 --> 00:01:45.376
Big image AIs work the same way, just with millions of examples

26
00:01:45.426 --> 00:01:47.150
and much bigger models.

27
00:01:48.600 --> 00:01:49.828
Let us recap.

28
00:01:49.878 --> 00:01:53.858
Choose groups and draw labelled examples.

29
00:01:53.908 --> 00:01:57.299
Press Train, then try new drawings.

30
00:01:57.349 --> 00:02:02.508
Low confidence means the model needs better examples.

31
00:02:02.558 --> 00:02:07.030
Next: How your AI decides: nearest neighbours.
